! FatesNvp: run FATES with the moss (non-vascular phototroph) PFT enabled.
!
! The switch and the parameter file travel together: with use_fates_moss true, FATES
! requires a parameter file whose fates_litterclass dimension is 8, and with it false it
! requires 6. Setting either alone aborts at initialization, by design.
!
! use_bedrock is deliberately absent: it lives in the FatesALP2* testmods.
!
! This is the general-purpose moss testmod. FatesMossParams is identical to it today but
! stays minimal, because its only job is to exercise the 8-litterclass parameter file
! against a non-moss fsurdat. Do not consolidate the two: new moss history variables are
! added HERE as they are implemented, which is what will make them diverge.
!
! Those additions MUST use the append form:
!     hist_fincl1 += 'FATES_SOME_MOSS_VARIABLE'
! A plain `hist_fincl1 = ...` would REPLACE, not extend. CIME applies testmods in order and
! later ones win (cime/CIME/user_mod_support.py), and the nocomp test composes this testmod
! after clm/Fates, which sets hist_empty_htapes plus the 71-variable FATES list. Assigning
! here would silently wipe FATES_FUEL_AMOUNT, FATES_BURNFRAC and the rest -- on the only two
! tests that run SPITFIRE. It would look harmless on the SP tests, which do not include
! clm/Fates.

use_fates_moss = .true.
fates_paramfile = '$SRCROOT/src/fates/parameter_files/fates_params_moss.json'

hist_fincl1 += 'FATES_LIVEMOSS_FUEL'
hist_fincl1 += 'FATES_MOSS_FINES'
hist_fincl1 += 'FATES_MOSS_FWET'
hist_fincl1 += 'FATES_MOSS_FWET_SOIL'
hist_fincl1 += 'FATES_MOSS_FWET_CANOPY'
hist_fincl1 += 'FATES_MOSS_WETNESS_SCALER'
hist_fincl1 += 'FATES_MOSS_HEIGHT'

! Existing FATES per-PFT and per-fuel-class diagnostics that the moss science
! checks need read out for the moss PFT and for fuel classes 7 (live moss) and 8 (dead
! moss). They are not moss-specific variables, which is why they are not covered by the
! block above.
!
! They are requested here because the two SPITFIRE-enabled tests -- the I2000Clm60Fates
! nocomp entries, the only ones where fire runs at all -- set hist_empty_htapes via
! clm/Fates, and clm/Fates's hist_fincl1 lists none of these. Without these lines those
! two tests emit nothing usable for moss fuel loading, moss fuel moisture, moss GPP or
! moss mortality.
!
! FATES_LEAFC_PF and FATES_CROWNAREA_PF are here for the moss leaf-biomass allometry:
! leaf carbon per m2 land area, and the crown area that converts it to per m2 crown
! area.
!
! On the FATES-SP tests these come back as zeros -- the fire ones because SP mode cannot
! run SPITFIRE (build-namelist makes fates_spitfire_mode > 0 fatal under use_fates_sp),
! the mortality ones because SP bypasses the demographic paths. hist_fincl1 wins over
! hist_fexcl1, so the fire entries appear on the SP tapes despite fates_sp excluding
! them. Zeros there are the correct reading, not a defect.
!
! FATES_NOCOMP_PATCHAREA_PF is registered only when nocomp is on (nocomp_if in
! FatesHistoryInterfaceMod). Every test composing this testmod today has nocomp on -- SP
! forces it, and the fire tests compose FatesColdNoCompFixedBioGeo. If this testmod is
! ever composed with full competition, drop that line: naming an unregistered field in
! hist_fincl1 is a hard endrun, not a warning.

hist_fincl1 += 'FATES_FUEL_MOISTURE_FC'
hist_fincl1 += 'FATES_FUEL_AMOUNT_FC'
hist_fincl1 += 'FATES_FUEL_BURNT_BURNFRAC_FC'
hist_fincl1 += 'FATES_GPP_PF'
hist_fincl1 += 'FATES_LEAFC_PF'
hist_fincl1 += 'FATES_CROWNAREA_PF'
hist_fincl1 += 'FATES_NOCOMP_PATCHAREA_PF'
hist_fincl1 += 'FATES_MORTALITY_HYDRAULIC_PF'
hist_fincl1 += 'FATES_MORTALITY_TERMINATION_PF'

! Moss leaf and stem area index. Each is the per-PFT sum of ccohort%treelai (resp.
! ccohort%treesai) times ccohort%c_area*AREA_INV over every cohort of the PFT, in
! every canopy layer and size class.
!
! Note the normalization: these are per m2 LAND area. Dividing FATES_LAI_PF by
! FATES_CROWNAREA_PF recovers ccohort%treelai itself, per m2 CROWN area, which is the
! quantity the moss leaf-biomass allometry is reasoned about in.

hist_fincl1 += 'FATES_LAI_PF'
hist_fincl1 += 'FATES_SAI_PF'
